+- FR-1: WHEN a successful input data owner is copied by ordinaryGo structvaluecopy, all copies SHALL share one consumptionidentity; at most one successful byte handoff is permitted.
+- FR-2: WHEN32concurrent callers consume the original and/orvaluecopies, a sharedmutex SHALL serialize validation and handoff without dataraces; every later validattempt rejects after successful consumption.
+- FR-3: The owner SHALL retain exact original9-fieldbinding,payloadhash,length and cancellationcontext in sharedstate; nil/malformed/foreign/corrupt/overcapacity owners SHALLdeny. Failedforeignbinding attempts before successfulconsumption remain retryable to preserve the existingoriginalpositive contract. Cancellation at/after handoffattempt neverreopens consumedstate.
